[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/verifiable-ai-guarantee-composition/issues/comments/6257432548","html_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/verifiable-ai-guarantee-composition/pull/5#issuecomment-6257432548","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/verifiable-ai-guarantee-composition/issues/5","id":6257432548,"node_id":"IC_kwDOVMZGKc8AAAABdPjX5A","user":{"login":"pipavlo82","id":212635108,"node_id":"U_kgDODKyN5A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/212635108?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82","html_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-19T01:02:01Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T01:02:01Z","body":"@babyblueviper1\r\n\r\nIndependent cold review completed against\r\na61ffd26b799d409d173654174603e14c17d1245.\r\n\r\nVerdict: HOLD — two reproducible admission-boundary\r\nfindings.\r\n\r\nF1 — Mutable authorization result (P2)\r\n\r\nIn the real self-judgment witness, changing only\r\nC.authorized from false to true causes admit()\r\nto accept the result, even though C.status and\r\nO14 remain REFUTED.\r\n\r\nThis means admission currently trusts a mutable\r\nauthorization flag without establishing the\r\nauthenticity or correctness of the underlying\r\nverification result.\r\n\r\nThe consumer must either:\r\n- Recompute the decision from trusted evidence, or\r\n- Verify an authenticated result bound to the\r\n  complete claim, scenario, contract and scope.\r\n\r\nA positive authorization flag alone is insufficient.\r\n\r\nF2 — Scenario binding (P2)\r\n\r\nRemoving or modifying binding.scenario is accepted\r\nby admit().\r\n\r\nThe contract_sha256 still identifies the correct\r\ncontract, but the result can carry inconsistent\r\nscenario metadata without being rejected.\r\n\r\nAdmission should verify that binding.scenario\r\nmatches the exact scenario declared by the\r\nconsumer's contract.\r\n\r\nF3 — Unconsumed-field coverage limitation\r\n\r\nA predicate can read a claim field without\r\nactually validating its value, causing that field\r\nto be marked as consumed.\r\n\r\nAn additional isolated mutation witness reproduced\r\nthis behavior.\r\n\r\nThis is a coverage limitation rather than a\r\nconfirmed bypass in the unmodified implementation.\r\n\r\nPlease either strengthen the consumption contract\r\nor explicitly document that field consumption\r\nmeans observation, not semantic validation.\r\n\r\nConfirmed by independent execution:\r\n\r\n- O14 behaves as declared.\r\n- 13/13 v4.1 tests PASS in normal/repeat/-O.\r\n- 6/6 existing mutation controls KILLED.\r\n- 3/3 additional mutation witnesses KILLED.\r\n- Historical v4: 24 tests PASS, 44 mutants KILLED.\r\n- Independent EIP-712 signature recovery completed.\r\n- Native zkIE proof replay completed.\r\n- SHA-256 inventory: 4,649 files verified.\r\n- Deterministic results across execution modes.\r\n\r\nTwo reporting/integration issues also remain:\r\n\r\n- The PR reports 58 scenarios, but 57 were\r\n  observed during independent reproduction.\r\n- GitHub CI is currently action_required,\r\n  not green, and the existing workflows\r\n  do not execute the v4.1 suite.\r\n\r\nRequested before another review:\r\n\r\n1. Add isolated regression witnesses for F1/F2.\r\n2. Add load-bearing mutation controls for both.\r\n3. Ensure admission cannot be authorized by\r\n   modifying an unauthenticated result.\r\n4. Bind scenario metadata to the exact contract.\r\n5. Clarify the unconsumed-field limitation.\r\n6. Correct the scenario count.\r\n7. Include v4.1 in GitHub CI.\r\n8. Preserve all original v4 evidence and\r\n   historical mutation results.\r\n\r\nThe findings concern the experimental\r\nauthorization boundary, not a demonstrated\r\nvulnerability in zkIE, WYRIWE or ERC-8404.\r\n\r\nNo source changes, commits, pushes or merges\r\nwere performed during this review.\r\n\r\nHolding LGTM until F1/F2 are independently\r\nreproduced as closed, with their regression\r\ncontrols confirmed load-bearing.\r\n\r\nThanks for the contribution and for keeping\r\nthe changes isolated from the original v4.","author_association":"OWNER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/verifiable-ai-guarantee-composition/issues/comments/6257432548/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/verifiable-ai-guarantee-composition/issues/comments/6257811443","html_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/verifiable-ai-guarantee-composition/pull/5#issuecomment-6257811443","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/verifiable-ai-guarantee-composition/issues/5","id":6257811443,"node_id":"IC_kwDOVMZGKc8AAAABdP6f8w","user":{"login":"babyblueviper1","id":241826547,"node_id":"U_kgDODmn68w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/241826547?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1","html_url":"https://github.com/babyblueviper1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-19T01:37:52Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T01:37:52Z","body":"Thanks, all reproduced. Fixed in c14d96b. No v4 file changed; the manifest diff is the v4.1 entries plus the new workflow.\n\n**F1/F2.** The signature is now `admit(result, evidence, contract, claim_type)`. It recomputes C from the evidence and refuses any presented C that differs from it (status, authorized, every binding field). Then it recomputes the digest from the consumer's contract and checks the claim type. The binding is derived from the contract object, so an equal digest also fixes `binding.scenario` and `binding.claim_type` to that contract.\n\nWhile fixing these I found a third case that the first `admit` also let through: `positive_replay`'s result with its whole binding rewritten to revision 3's scenario, claim type and digest. The recompute refuses it as well.\n\nWitnesses. Each one was admitted by the a61ffd2 `admit` and is refused now:\n- `reused_tampered_authorized`: only `C.authorized` set to true (C.status and O14 stay REFUTED)\n- `reused_tampered_scenario`: `binding.scenario` removed (the unit test also covers a changed value)\n- `reused_forged_binding`: the whole binding rewritten\n\n**Mutation controls.** Each witness has its own physical mutant on the recompute check, with `control_output_same_contract` as the positive control. Result: 9/9 KILLED in normal and `-O` (the 6 earlier mutants plus these 3). Source and catalog were restored byte-exact.\n\n**F3.** The README and the model docstring now say it directly: consumption means observation, not semantic validation. A predicate that reads a field without testing it marks the field consumed.\n\n**Counts.** You're right: 57 rows (54 carried + 3 new), not 58. That was our error and the README now says so. Current numbers: 7 reuse cases, C false authorizations 0/53, false admissions 0/5, 16 tests in normal and `-O`.\n\n**CI.** `.github/workflows/coverage-v4_1.yml` runs the comparison, the tests in both modes and the mutations in both modes. The `action_required` state is GitHub holding workflows on a fork PR until a maintainer approves the run, so that step is yours.\n\nv4 evidence and the historical v4 mutation results are untouched.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/verifiable-ai-guarantee-composition/issues/comments/6257811443/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/verifiable-ai-guarantee-composition/issues/comments/6258448494","html_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/verifiable-ai-guarantee-composition/pull/5#issuecomment-6258448494","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/verifiable-ai-guarantee-composition/issues/5","id":6258448494,"node_id":"IC_kwDOVMZGKc8AAAABdQhYbg","user":{"login":"pipavlo82","id":212635108,"node_id":"U_kgDODKyN5A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/212635108?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82","html_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-19T02:36:23Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T02:36:23Z","body":"@babyblueviper1\n\nLGTM — the updated implementation closes both previously reported admission-boundary findings.\n\nThe mutable authorization flag and scenario-binding bypasses are now rejected through independent recomputation at admission. The additional cross-contract and claim-type controls strengthen the boundary.\n\nThanks for addressing the findings and preserving the original v4 evidence.\n\nApproved for integration into the v4 research branch, pending the combined composition review with #6. **No merge yet.**\n\nReview scope: `c14d96b0a63fceba02b2cb4469d5b3228ae46612`. Local independent replay passed 16 tests, 57 scenarios and 7 reuse controls in normal/repeat/Python -O; the 9 mutation controls were reproduced with exact restoration. GitHub CI is still `action_required`, so no green remote CI is claimed. The documented read-tracking limitation remains: observing a field read does not prove that its value was validated. Merge must wait for the combined #5 + #6 review and successful CI.\n","author_association":"OWNER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/verifiable-ai-guarantee-composition/issues/comments/6258448494/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]